      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_9b84c578b609af749848e61bcf1b79f13dfcf59b89015a08ff98f0f6fad93b9c",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "In the easy half-plane, diagonalization is exact enough that interval length is the only growing scale. Absolute convergence permits every rearrangement and bounds accumulated near-diagonal interactions.",
