    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1b1337f41599957ef1814a7bed3102dc3fbadf88c8938f8c43eb0152f237fc14",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source exhibits different proof interfaces on opposite sides of the fourth-to-higher-moment boundary. For the fourth moment, Gaussian smoothing makes a Bruggeman-Kuznetsov transformation to explicit Maass-spectral data available. For k at least 3, random-matrix heuristics predict asymptotics but no such asymptotic is proved even under RH; in the first higher case, the source identifies a ternary additive-divisor conjecture as sufficient for the expected sixth-moment bound. This is a concrete contrast between an available spectral representation and an unresolved additive-correlation input, not a claim that every higher moment has been reduced in the same way.",
