    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_632b0a6199bff9d6433ad5b3a3b92aff927a8fd8a291b38751499da77c00af8f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source treats lower and upper short-interval moment bounds through different extremal mechanisms. For the lower bound, analyticity and a rapidly decaying residue kernel transport a nonvanishing value from a safe half-plane and optimization prevents the interval average from collapsing. For the upper bound, the sharp logarithmic exponent is obtained by measuring rare large values of log|zeta|, weighting their level sets by the corresponding powers of |zeta|, and optimizing the competition between exponential weight and tail decay.",
