    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6dc785fc8803cfa49f7237664cb6bd5210a198f46ecc0f59a9f3cf772225049a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, the large-value proof is a three-stage reduction. A smoothed von Mangoldt majorant, prime-power removal, and a split at z turn a large log|zeta| event into the forced largeness of one of two prime Dirichlet polynomials. High even moments and Markov's inequality then bound those two event measures, with the moment order r chosen separately by deviation regime subject to x^r<=H. Finally, dyadic level-set weighting and quadratic optimization convert the resulting tails into the k^2 logarithmic moment exponent.",
